  "summary": "@inetafrica/open-claudia ships Telegram-bot exfiltration and shell-executing endpoints",
  "details": "The package ships multiple JavaScript modules that combine child_process execution, filesystem enumeration, and outbound HTTPS to hardcoded destinations. health.js and setup.js contain hardcoded calls to https://api.telegram.org (Telegram Bot API) reached from top-level scripts that also read process.env, process.platform, and process.version and shell out via child_process. bot.js and core/handlers.js perform similar patterns, invoking commands such as whoami and hostname alongside HTTPS POSTs. core/scheduler.js spawns \"sh\" for shell execution. test-tool-guard.js issues curl calls to https://central.inet.africa. The combination of hardcoded Telegram Bot API endpoints, host-identifier collection (whoami/hostname/os/process.env), shell-command execution, and filesystem reads reachable from setup and health scripts is consistent with a Telegram-bot-based command-and-control / exfiltration channel operated against the machine that installs or runs the package.",
